1
00:00:10,710 --> 00:00:14,476
Ah, the great pact of Nottingham, hm?

2
00:00:14,547 --> 00:00:16,572
All drawn up and ready for signature,

3
00:00:16,649 --> 00:00:19,015
safe in your quarters?

4
00:00:19,085 --> 00:00:20,416
Good, good.

5
00:00:21,955 --> 00:00:25,391
- And you've told nobody about your work?
- The scribe is mute, my lord.

6
00:00:25,458 --> 00:00:27,016
Mute?

7
00:00:28,661 --> 00:00:29,889
Are we sure?

8
00:00:31,931 --> 00:00:33,899
Oh, look! Look!

9
00:00:33,967 --> 00:00:37,926
Look, the black knights
on their way to the castle to sign the pact.

10
00:00:47,747 --> 00:00:49,408
Now we're sure.

11
00:01:04,197 --> 00:01:06,688
This what you're looking for?

12
00:01:08,168 --> 00:01:09,294
Your blood money?

13
00:01:09,369 --> 00:01:13,066
Betray your friends for a few measly pennies?

14
00:01:13,139 --> 00:01:14,128
Traitor!

15
00:01:14,207 --> 00:01:17,233
Look, I'm sorry, all right? I'm really sorry.

16
00:01:18,411 --> 00:01:19,776
I never wanted...

17
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:44,131
- Is that who I think it was?
- The black knights headed for Nottingham.

18
00:01:44,204 --> 00:01:45,933
What are they up to?

19
00:01:46,005 --> 00:01:47,836
I'm going in.

20
00:01:48,741 --> 00:01:50,572
- What about Allan?
- Forget him.

21
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:53,177
He's dead to us.

22
00:01:54,681 --> 00:01:56,239
Meet back at the camp in one hour.

23
00:01:56,316 --> 00:01:59,774
Well, you can't just decide
to go like this and go.

24
00:01:59,853 --> 00:02:01,650
Without planning, without us.

25
00:02:01,721 --> 00:02:04,952
- Yes, I can.
- It's the black knights!

26
00:02:08,094 --> 00:02:09,459
Why does he do this?

27
00:02:11,131 --> 00:02:14,532
Why does he always, always do this?

28
00:03:00,313 --> 00:03:02,247
What are these in aid of, Sir Guy?

29
00:03:02,982 --> 00:03:05,348
A bit of color... for you.

30
00:03:06,886 --> 00:03:09,980
I was wondering if you'd accompany me
to the celebrations today.

31
00:03:10,056 --> 00:03:12,354
- What are we celebrating?
- The King's birthday.

32
00:03:14,527 --> 00:03:18,088
- What are we really celebrating?
- Does it matter?

33
00:03:22,135 --> 00:03:24,626
It's the signing of an important document.

34
00:03:24,704 --> 00:03:27,229
Something tells me it is a document
which I won't approve of.

35
00:03:27,307 --> 00:03:31,710
Well, Marian, you should approve, because
this document brings me closer to real power.

36
00:03:33,213 --> 00:03:35,909
And that, in turn, benefits you.

37
00:03:36,549 --> 00:03:39,017
Could benefit you,

38
00:03:39,085 --> 00:03:40,450
in time.

39
00:03:43,389 --> 00:03:46,119
Meanwhile there's a
pretty dress in it for you.

40
00:03:46,192 --> 00:03:47,557
Am I so easily won?

41
00:03:48,595 --> 00:03:51,325
You must be the least
easily won woman in England.

42
00:03:52,732 --> 00:03:55,394
Well, if that's my reputation,

43
00:03:55,468 --> 00:03:58,631
then perhaps nobody will mind
if I do not attend...

44
00:03:58,705 --> 00:03:59,729
Choose a dress.

45
00:04:01,474 --> 00:04:02,771
Guy!

46
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:11,079
- What are you doing here?
- Just dropping in on you.

47
00:04:11,150 --> 00:04:12,640
So...

48
00:04:12,719 --> 00:04:14,778
the black knights are assembling.

49
00:04:14,854 --> 00:04:18,915
Did you hear Gisborne?
They're signing an important document.

50
00:04:18,992 --> 00:04:21,654
- Who died?
- Oh, the Sheriff's scribe.

51
00:04:21,728 --> 00:04:24,754
- Fell from the battlements.
- Outlived his usefulness.

52
00:04:24,831 --> 00:04:25,923
What?

53
00:04:25,999 --> 00:04:28,832
Dead scribes, black knights.

54
00:04:28,901 --> 00:04:31,870
Something tells me
we have to find this document.

55
00:04:45,585 --> 00:04:48,816
I'm not being funny, but your guards...

56
00:04:48,888 --> 00:04:50,355
Useless.

57
00:04:55,695 --> 00:04:58,755
- You need smart people on your team.
- Oh, and that's you, is it?

58
00:04:58,831 --> 00:05:02,130
- Well...
- Hood found you out?

59
00:05:04,704 --> 00:05:05,671
Maybe.

60
00:05:07,273 --> 00:05:08,638
Don't insult me.

61
00:05:12,612 --> 00:05:13,977
All right. I need your help.

62
00:05:15,682 --> 00:05:18,014
I've lost everything cos I helped you.

63
00:05:18,084 --> 00:05:20,450
- So you owe me.
- I owe you nothing.

64
00:05:21,688 --> 00:05:23,519
I paid you.

65
00:05:24,791 --> 00:05:26,019
Take me on, Guy. Come on.

66
00:05:27,260 --> 00:05:28,921
You won't regret it.

67
00:05:30,396 --> 00:05:32,956
Go and get one of my servants
to give you some food.

68
00:05:36,803 --> 00:05:37,770
Oh, nice.

69
00:05:37,837 --> 00:05:40,533
Yeah. Where are you off to, then?

70
00:05:42,942 --> 00:05:46,378
Get yourself cleaned up.
Come and find me in the castle.

71
00:06:01,127 --> 00:06:03,288
This is it, the scribe's room.

72
00:06:13,539 --> 00:06:15,268
- Better get a move on, then.
- Yeah.

73
00:06:16,376 --> 00:06:18,469
Down at the front gate again on guard.

74
00:06:18,544 --> 00:06:21,342
Doesn't like
to be kept waiting, does he?

75
00:06:24,584 --> 00:06:27,883
Robin! This isn't the time.

76
00:06:29,856 --> 00:06:31,289
Will that work?

77
00:06:31,357 --> 00:06:32,756
Trust me.

78
00:06:33,926 --> 00:06:35,450
I've done this before.

79
00:06:35,528 --> 00:06:37,257
With which girl's hairpin?

80
00:06:49,542 --> 00:06:51,908
The great pact of Nottingham.

81
00:06:53,513 --> 00:06:57,142
<i>"We, the undersigned, by the affixing
of our seals of office and nobility,</i>

82
00:06:57,216 --> 00:07:00,151
<i>"hereby undertake
to remove King Richard from the throne.</i>

83
00:07:00,219 --> 00:07:01,811
<i>"By his absence from these shores</i>

84
00:07:01,888 --> 00:07:04,652
<i>he has demonstrated
a scant regard for his subjects. "</i>

85
00:07:04,724 --> 00:07:06,885
- This is outrageous.
- "We further undertake

86
00:07:06,959 --> 00:07:11,919
"to replace the said Richard with his
brother John, Prince of the Realm. "

87
00:07:11,998 --> 00:07:15,161
The Sheriff is making the black knights
sign their allegiance.

88
00:07:15,234 --> 00:07:16,701
This is a traitors' charter.

89
00:07:18,504 --> 00:07:21,098
Looks like the Sheriff
has made some new friends.

90
00:07:21,174 --> 00:07:22,573
Buckingham, Spencer.

91
00:07:23,709 --> 00:07:24,676
Winchester?

92
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:28,641
Surely not. He's an old friend of my father.

93
00:07:31,384 --> 00:07:32,817
When the pact is signed,

94
00:07:32,885 --> 00:07:36,719
there can be no going back for our friends.

95
00:07:36,789 --> 00:07:38,154
Do you know something?

96
00:07:38,224 --> 00:07:41,557
I may change the habit of a lifetime
and enjoy this party.

97
00:08:06,853 --> 00:08:07,820
Nobody here.

98
00:08:17,597 --> 00:08:21,863
Look at this - the color, the detail,
the tone texture.

99
00:08:21,934 --> 00:08:24,266
This man was a true artist.

100
00:08:26,405 --> 00:08:29,033
I'm sorry I killed him now.

101
00:08:29,108 --> 00:08:31,838
A clue? No.

102
00:08:33,412 --> 00:08:34,879
Gone.

103
00:08:43,189 --> 00:08:44,156
Go, go!

104
00:08:45,191 --> 00:08:48,524
I cannot believe Winchester would willingly
be involved in this revolt.

105
00:08:48,594 --> 00:08:50,528
Winchester controls the south coast.

106
00:08:50,596 --> 00:08:52,826
The Sheriff wants to
intercept the King's landing.

107
00:08:52,899 --> 00:08:56,062
But Winchester?
I've known him since we were boys.

108
00:08:56,135 --> 00:08:58,330
The Sheriff must have got to him.

109
00:08:58,404 --> 00:09:01,066
- Good.
- Good?

110
00:09:01,140 --> 00:09:03,506
If the Sheriff can get to him, then so can I.

111
00:09:04,677 --> 00:09:06,406
Edward, I'll be back.

112
00:09:06,479 --> 00:09:09,812
And when I get back,
I will get you out of this place.

113
00:09:10,917 --> 00:09:13,147
What should I do?

114
00:09:13,219 --> 00:09:16,279
Be meek and obedient, my child.

115
00:09:16,355 --> 00:09:18,346
Until I know more.

116
00:09:19,492 --> 00:09:21,016
Jailer, confession's over.

117
00:09:33,372 --> 00:09:34,896
Why have we stopped?

118
00:09:35,808 --> 00:09:37,366
Ah. Move it.

119
00:09:39,812 --> 00:09:42,872
My Lord Winchester, I am a friend.

120
00:09:42,949 --> 00:09:46,316
I know you're coming to Nottingham
to sign the Sheriff's pact.

121
00:09:46,385 --> 00:09:48,478
I don't know what you're talking about.

122
00:09:49,522 --> 00:09:52,582
My name is Robin Hood.
We haven't got time for games.

123
00:09:52,658 --> 00:09:54,489
Robin, forgive me, I...

124
00:09:54,560 --> 00:09:56,050
I have to be careful.

125
00:09:56,128 --> 00:09:59,461
We have a mutual friend
- Sir Edward, the former Sheriff of Nottingham.

126
00:09:59,532 --> 00:10:01,659
- How is he?
- He's in the Sheriff's dungeons.

127
00:10:01,734 --> 00:10:02,701
Good God.

128
00:10:03,803 --> 00:10:06,795
- Well, what can we do?
- First we need to kill this pact.

129
00:10:06,872 --> 00:10:10,205
Spencer and Buckingham
are signing under duress too.

130
00:10:10,276 --> 00:10:13,268
Now if, at the moment of signing,
you were to refuse,

131
00:10:13,346 --> 00:10:16,577
the black knights would lose faith
and the Sheriff's pact would be history.

132
00:10:16,649 --> 00:10:19,209
That's dangerous.
The Sheriff would turn his men on me.

133
00:10:19,285 --> 00:10:21,446
Well, that's where I
come in. You need support.

134
00:10:22,655 --> 00:10:25,249
Forgive me, I'm... I'm a peace-loving man.

135
00:10:25,324 --> 00:10:28,191
I want stability and the Sheriff
and his knights are offering that.

136
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:30,387
What they don't know

137
00:10:30,463 --> 00:10:32,658
is that I've already sent
a messenger to the King -

138
00:10:32,732 --> 00:10:34,427
Roger of Stoke.

139
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:36,491
By now the King will know about this plot.

140
00:10:36,569 --> 00:10:38,867
When he returns to England,
the first thing he'll do

141
00:10:38,938 --> 00:10:40,633
is crush the black knights.

142
00:10:42,375 --> 00:10:47,142
If you love peace, do anything
but do not sign the Sheriff's pact.

143
00:10:50,716 --> 00:10:51,876
Uh-huh.

144
00:10:51,951 --> 00:10:53,077
Count me in.

145
00:10:59,125 --> 00:11:00,092
Right, lads.

146
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:03,451
Work to do. We're going to the castle.

147
00:11:03,529 --> 00:11:07,021
- Why?
- Why? To save England.

148
00:11:07,099 --> 00:11:08,760
Marian and her father.

149
00:11:08,834 --> 00:11:12,065
The Sheriff is hosting a celebration
for the King's birthday except...

150
00:11:12,138 --> 00:11:15,232
it's really a celebration
for the black knights signing the pact.

151
00:11:15,307 --> 00:11:19,243
Will, you need to find us a way
of getting into this party.

152
00:11:19,311 --> 00:11:21,336
- I've already done it.
- How?

153
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:24,748
The castle announced this party weeks ago.

154
00:11:24,817 --> 00:11:28,275
Put out a call for entertainers and players.

155
00:11:28,354 --> 00:11:32,916
Well, it gave me an idea
and... I've been busy.

156
00:11:32,992 --> 00:11:33,981
It's a harp.

157
00:11:37,063 --> 00:11:39,122
It's a recurve bow.

158
00:11:39,198 --> 00:11:40,631
Djaq.

159
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:42,895
It's a flute.

160
00:11:43,803 --> 00:11:45,930
- What's this do?
- Much, don't...

161
00:11:51,410 --> 00:11:52,536
Sorry.

162
00:11:52,611 --> 00:11:54,101
This is for you.

163
00:11:57,383 --> 00:11:59,908
Will, you're a genius, and a magician.

164
00:11:59,985 --> 00:12:01,213
You're brilliant.

165
00:12:01,287 --> 00:12:04,256
You crafty craftsman.

166
00:12:04,323 --> 00:12:06,621
- What about me?
- Ah.

167
00:12:08,127 --> 00:12:09,754
These are for you.

168
00:12:10,963 --> 00:12:12,828
Bells. What do they do?

169
00:12:14,366 --> 00:12:16,561
Oh, they're... they're just bells.

170
00:12:19,171 --> 00:12:20,138
Thanks.

171
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:34,583
Delighted to welcome Harold of Winchester

172
00:12:34,653 --> 00:12:37,486
to join our celebrations
for the King's birthday.

173
00:12:37,556 --> 00:12:39,217
Thank you, Marian.

174
00:12:40,793 --> 00:12:43,819
- We sign in one hour.
- Marvelous.

175
00:12:43,896 --> 00:12:47,423
I was ungrateful earlier. I'm sorry.

176
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:49,229
I was overbearing.

177
00:12:49,301 --> 00:12:51,496
Could I have a word in
private with you first?

178
00:12:51,570 --> 00:12:54,095
And I'd like to talk
to your predecessor, Sir Edward, if I may.

179
00:12:54,173 --> 00:12:57,006
Yes, well, Sir Edward is...
How shall I put it? Indisposed.

180
00:12:57,076 --> 00:12:58,065
In what way?

181
00:12:58,144 --> 00:13:00,738
- He's in the dungeons.
- No, really?

182
00:13:00,813 --> 00:13:03,407
He's loyal to the King.

183
00:13:03,482 --> 00:13:06,007
And also a right royal pain in the derrière.

184
00:13:06,085 --> 00:13:08,485
I'd still like to talk to him
if you have no objections.

185
00:13:08,554 --> 00:13:12,115
Yes, well, it can be arranged.

186
00:13:13,392 --> 00:13:15,587
Gisborne will show you to your quarters.

187
00:13:15,661 --> 00:13:16,889
Keep your eye on him.

188
00:13:19,565 --> 00:13:21,533
This way, my Lord.

189
00:13:26,172 --> 00:13:28,834
My Lord, this way.

190
00:13:28,908 --> 00:13:30,307
Ah, yes.

191
00:13:35,848 --> 00:13:38,316
Reason for visit? Security check.

192
00:13:38,384 --> 00:13:40,409
No knives, no weapons in the castle.

193
00:13:42,521 --> 00:13:45,513
We're the band, the minstrels.

194
00:13:54,967 --> 00:13:56,730
- Will... Allan.
- Much.

195
00:14:00,973 --> 00:14:03,806
I'm Sir Guy's man. Can you let me pass?

196
00:14:03,876 --> 00:14:05,173
In you go.

197
00:14:08,214 --> 00:14:10,011
What's he doing here?

198
00:14:10,082 --> 00:14:11,640
He's being Sir Guy's man.

199
00:14:11,717 --> 00:14:14,845
- Unbelievable.
- Did you see what he was wearing?

200
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:17,218
Unbelievable.
Whose is this?

201
00:14:21,994 --> 00:14:23,222
I said, "Whose is this?"

202
00:14:25,297 --> 00:14:26,264
It's mine.

203
00:14:30,369 --> 00:14:32,166
Oh, a bit's come off. I'm sorry.

204
00:14:33,505 --> 00:14:35,939
That's all right. I'm good with wood.

205
00:14:39,411 --> 00:14:40,435
Er, bells, mate.

206
00:15:01,667 --> 00:15:04,636
You know what to do.
I'm off to see Winchester. Wait here.

207
00:15:07,706 --> 00:15:10,266
Oh, ha! Hey...

208
00:15:21,153 --> 00:15:23,451
What?

209
00:15:25,324 --> 00:15:27,588
I had to put something on, didn't I?

210
00:15:27,660 --> 00:15:31,653
I suppose you want me
to introduce you to the Sheriff now, do you?

211
00:15:31,730 --> 00:15:33,357
Yeah.

212
00:15:33,465 --> 00:15:35,023
Wait through there.

213
00:15:40,572 --> 00:15:43,598
Go in there and get yourselves ready.

214
00:15:43,676 --> 00:15:45,075
Er, of course. We'll...

215
00:15:45,144 --> 00:15:47,476
We'll go in there and... tune up.

216
00:15:51,116 --> 00:15:53,584
We can't possibly go in there. Allan.

217
00:15:53,652 --> 00:15:55,950
Why not?

218
00:15:56,055 --> 00:15:58,819
We... never share dressing rooms.

219
00:15:58,891 --> 00:16:01,086
You are already dressed.

220
00:16:01,160 --> 00:16:03,128
It's a principle.

221
00:16:03,195 --> 00:16:04,753
We're artists.

222
00:16:07,666 --> 00:16:09,065
He's the drummer.

223
00:16:16,608 --> 00:16:20,044
- My men are safely in the castle.
- I heard you could walk through walls.

224
00:16:20,112 --> 00:16:23,309
Your meeting will no doubt take place
in the war room. I'll be there.

225
00:16:23,382 --> 00:16:26,840
- It will be strictly black knights only.
- Then I shall be a black knight.

226
00:16:26,919 --> 00:16:29,581
- Confident.
- Determined.

227
00:16:29,655 --> 00:16:32,249
My men will be waiting outside the war room.

228
00:16:32,324 --> 00:16:34,918
When you've said your piece,
I'll cover for you. You run.

229
00:16:34,994 --> 00:16:38,452
- My men will secure your safe exit.
- Thank you, but what about you?

230
00:16:39,465 --> 00:16:41,626
Well, I can walk through walls. Remember?

231
00:16:42,935 --> 00:16:44,493
- Good luck.
- You too.

232
00:16:44,570 --> 00:16:46,094
And thank you.

233
00:16:52,778 --> 00:16:54,109
Tell me something.

234
00:16:54,179 --> 00:16:59,207
What do you know about a messenger sent by
Robin Hood to the King telling him of our plans?

235
00:16:59,284 --> 00:17:01,047
Roger of Stoke?

236
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:02,781
Oh, don't worry about him.

237
00:17:02,855 --> 00:17:05,119
- He got lost en route.
- Well done.

238
00:17:06,458 --> 00:17:08,824
If I might be allowed
to speak to Sir Edward in private?

239
00:17:12,765 --> 00:17:13,732
Edward.

240
00:17:13,799 --> 00:17:16,290
Harry, my old friend!

241
00:17:16,368 --> 00:17:17,995
What has happened to you?

242
00:17:18,070 --> 00:17:19,435
Sit down.

243
00:17:22,408 --> 00:17:26,868
- I've had a visit from a friend of yours.
- Robin.

244
00:17:26,945 --> 00:17:28,435
Excellent.

245
00:17:28,514 --> 00:17:31,540
He advised me not to back the wrong horse.

246
00:17:31,617 --> 00:17:33,209
Mm-hm.

247
00:17:33,285 --> 00:17:36,311
- But then I look where you've ended up.
- Harry...

248
00:17:36,388 --> 00:17:40,222
I could back you, Edward,
and end up stuck in a cell with vermin.

249
00:17:40,292 --> 00:17:43,784
Or I could back the Sheriff
and just get richer and more powerful.

250
00:17:43,862 --> 00:17:45,921
Rats or riches?

251
00:17:45,998 --> 00:17:47,522
It's a tough choice.

252
00:17:47,599 --> 00:17:50,625
Harry, you cannot sign the pact.

253
00:17:50,702 --> 00:17:52,795
Oh, I will sign the pact.

254
00:17:52,871 --> 00:17:55,032
You are mad
if you think you can trust the Sheriff.

255
00:17:55,107 --> 00:17:56,131
Trust?

256
00:17:56,208 --> 00:17:57,641
No, no, no.

257
00:17:57,709 --> 00:17:59,404
I don't trust anyone.

258
00:17:59,478 --> 00:18:02,811
You taught me that
when you stole the woman I loved.

259
00:18:02,881 --> 00:18:04,508
Jailer.

260
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:05,607
Kate?

261
00:18:06,518 --> 00:18:08,679
She chose me, Harold, I didn't steal her.

262
00:18:08,754 --> 00:18:10,517
I was just thinking of her.

263
00:18:10,589 --> 00:18:14,320
I thought I saw her outside just now -
a young woman the very image of Kate.

264
00:18:16,929 --> 00:18:19,796
She's your daughter. Of course.

265
00:18:19,865 --> 00:18:22,197
She's her mother's double.

266
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:26,067
Well done, Edward. We wouldn't want her
inheriting your looks, now, would we?

267
00:18:30,075 --> 00:18:31,372
Oh, oh, oh.

268
00:18:32,978 --> 00:18:35,071
I've just had an idea.

269
00:18:35,147 --> 00:18:38,014
If I couldn't have the mother... Hm?

270
00:18:39,084 --> 00:18:42,247
What's her name, hm,
your little precious pea?

271
00:18:42,321 --> 00:18:44,846
- No.
- No? That's not a name now, is it?

272
00:18:44,923 --> 00:18:45,890
No!

273
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:48,256
Harry, she's got nothing to do with this.

274
00:18:48,327 --> 00:18:50,295
- Please.
- I don't think he likes me any more.

275
00:18:50,362 --> 00:18:53,331
Please!

276
00:19:04,610 --> 00:19:05,599
Harry.

277
00:19:05,677 --> 00:19:08,305
You wanted... a word.

278
00:19:11,116 --> 00:19:13,141
What was the word?

279
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:17,245
- Sussex.
- Sussex?

280
00:19:17,322 --> 00:19:18,687
Sussex.

281
00:19:20,926 --> 00:19:22,484
Sussex. Hm.

282
00:19:22,561 --> 00:19:24,051
I want it.

283
00:19:24,129 --> 00:19:25,460
Sussex?

284
00:19:26,398 --> 00:19:28,628
I hold the key to the success of your plan.

285
00:19:28,700 --> 00:19:31,066
Buckingham and Spencer are nervous.

286
00:19:31,136 --> 00:19:34,299
- They'll do as they're told.
- Not if they see me falter.

287
00:19:34,373 --> 00:19:38,707
Not if you don't have access to the south
coast where King Richard's most likely to land.

288
00:19:38,777 --> 00:19:42,508
I have therefore decided
my price for helping you is Sussex.

289
00:19:42,581 --> 00:19:44,344
Oh, and some of Surrey.

290
00:19:48,921 --> 00:19:50,684
Oh!

291
00:19:50,756 --> 00:19:53,554
Harry!

292
00:19:54,693 --> 00:19:57,218
Very good, very good.
Almost had me there.

293
00:19:57,296 --> 00:20:00,629
No, I'm serious. If you want this pact
signed today, it will cost you Sussex.

294
00:20:00,699 --> 00:20:02,894
- And some of Surrey.
- Surrey?

295
00:20:02,968 --> 00:20:05,095
- And the girl.
- What girl?

296
00:20:05,170 --> 00:20:06,330
- Er, Marian.
- No.

297
00:20:06,405 --> 00:20:10,603
- Shut up.
- You still gain Warwick, Lincoln and Cambridge.

298
00:20:10,676 --> 00:20:13,144
And some of Surrey.

299
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:15,271
Oh, and I have something to offer you -

300
00:20:15,347 --> 00:20:18,714
a little bonus, a little... sweetener.

301
00:20:18,784 --> 00:20:21,446
Still, if you're not playing...

302
00:20:46,778 --> 00:20:49,042
You get Sussex.

303
00:20:52,050 --> 00:20:54,416
I keep Surrey.

304
00:20:55,587 --> 00:20:58,317
Oh, you drive a hard bargain.

305
00:20:59,558 --> 00:21:01,458
- It's a deal.
- Marian stays.

306
00:21:01,526 --> 00:21:04,051
Not negotiable. Sorry, it's a personal thing.

307
00:21:04,129 --> 00:21:08,088
The girl and Sussex and then you sign.

308
00:21:09,768 --> 00:21:12,066
- Pleasure doing business with you.
- My Lord...

309
00:21:12,137 --> 00:21:14,332
- Harry?
- Mm?

310
00:21:14,406 --> 00:21:16,237
What was the sweetener?

311
00:21:16,308 --> 00:21:17,468
Later.

312
00:21:17,542 --> 00:21:20,306
You'll like it.

313
00:21:23,882 --> 00:21:26,908
- You cannot give him Marian.
- I have lost Sussex.

314
00:21:26,985 --> 00:21:28,475
Sussex!

315
00:21:28,553 --> 00:21:30,453
And all you can do is bleat about a girl!

316
00:21:31,456 --> 00:21:33,651
- I want a hanging.
- What?

317
00:21:33,725 --> 00:21:36,922
Find me somebody to hang.
I want to see somebody twitch.

318
00:21:36,995 --> 00:21:38,087
My Lord.

319
00:21:38,163 --> 00:21:40,495
- This man said you were going to see him.
- Not now.

320
00:21:40,565 --> 00:21:41,896
- You'll do.
- What for?

321
00:21:41,967 --> 00:21:43,264
- Hang him.
- What?

322
00:21:43,335 --> 00:21:44,597
- No, this man works for me.
- So?

323
00:21:44,670 --> 00:21:46,262
So, he was my spy in Hood's camp.

324
00:21:46,338 --> 00:21:47,896
- Was.
- Hood found him out.

325
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:51,101
- Well, he's served his purpose then.
- He might still prove useful.

326
00:21:51,176 --> 00:21:54,703
You are not listening to me, Gisborne.
Go and find that lady friend of yours.

327
00:21:54,780 --> 00:21:56,509
Take her to see the nice Lord Winchester,

328
00:21:56,581 --> 00:21:59,812
then bring him before me
with a hood over his head!

329
00:21:59,885 --> 00:22:01,648
Hang on a minute, I'm on your team now.

330
00:22:01,720 --> 00:22:03,620
And I can help, honest. Guy?

331
00:22:04,690 --> 00:22:07,818
La... di-da di-da!

332
00:22:10,162 --> 00:22:11,390
Guy?

333
00:22:11,463 --> 00:22:14,091
Hang on, just let me
say something here, right? Guy?

334
00:22:14,166 --> 00:22:16,191
- Come on, you can't be serious.
- Take him away.

335
00:22:16,268 --> 00:22:18,429
What? Guy, what are you doing?

336
00:22:31,049 --> 00:22:33,415
I'm not hungry.

337
00:22:33,485 --> 00:22:34,679
Robin!

338
00:22:34,753 --> 00:22:38,086
- Thank heavens.
- Sh. I haven't got much time.

339
00:22:38,156 --> 00:22:42,286
The Sheriff is about to have his meeting
and Winchester is going to refuse to sign.

340
00:22:42,361 --> 00:22:46,491
There'll be absolute chaos and in that chaos
I intend to come down and get you out.

341
00:22:49,201 --> 00:22:50,168
What?

342
00:22:50,268 --> 00:22:52,361
Winchester is going to sign.

343
00:22:53,405 --> 00:22:54,929
- He's a traitor.
- A traitor?

344
00:22:57,109 --> 00:22:59,270
And he wants Marian.

345
00:22:59,344 --> 00:23:01,904
Marian? What for?

346
00:23:01,980 --> 00:23:05,006
Revenge. Against me.

347
00:23:05,083 --> 00:23:09,019
- What?
- He thinks I took his woman

348
00:23:09,087 --> 00:23:10,850
so he's going to take my daughter.

349
00:23:14,593 --> 00:23:16,652
Robin?

350
00:23:19,064 --> 00:23:21,362
- Then I have no choice.
- What?

351
00:23:21,466 --> 00:23:23,730
What are you going to do?

352
00:23:26,271 --> 00:23:27,738
Godspeed, Edward.

353
00:23:31,576 --> 00:23:32,543
Guy?

354
00:23:32,611 --> 00:23:35,842
- Do me the courtesy of knocking.
- Get your possessions. You're leaving.

355
00:23:35,914 --> 00:23:37,245
- What?
- Now.

356
00:23:37,315 --> 00:23:38,441
Why?

357
00:23:38,517 --> 00:23:42,009
Winchester's made a deal with the Sheriff.
You've become part of a negotiation.

358
00:23:42,087 --> 00:23:45,488
- Pardon?
- Winchester wants you.

359
00:23:48,193 --> 00:23:51,356
- Tell him he can't have me.
- The Sheriff has agreed. I cannot protect you.

360
00:23:52,764 --> 00:23:54,061
Marian, listen to me.

361
00:23:54,132 --> 00:23:56,828
- You have to run now.
- I can't. My father.

362
00:23:56,902 --> 00:23:59,029
- I will take care of him.
- I cannot leave him.

363
00:23:59,104 --> 00:24:01,470
Why do you always resist me?
I'm attempting to help you.

364
00:24:01,540 --> 00:24:03,974
I know, I can see that, and I'm grateful.

365
00:24:04,075 --> 00:24:07,067
If the Sheriff knew I was doing this,
my own life would be in danger.

366
00:24:07,145 --> 00:24:09,306
Why do you work for him?

367
00:24:10,449 --> 00:24:11,916
I have nobody.

368
00:24:11,983 --> 00:24:14,611
- What, so you choose him?
- So I choose power.

369
00:24:14,686 --> 00:24:16,620
He is my route to position, standing.

370
00:24:16,688 --> 00:24:18,918
- He is mad, you know that.
- No.

371
00:24:18,990 --> 00:24:20,480
He is single-minded.

372
00:24:20,559 --> 00:24:23,926
He does not allow distractions
to pervert him from his course.

373
00:24:23,995 --> 00:24:26,725
Distractions? Like a little humanity?

374
00:24:26,798 --> 00:24:28,629
Humanity is weakness.

375
00:24:28,700 --> 00:24:30,361
You don't believe that.

376
00:24:32,337 --> 00:24:33,861
You must leave this place.

377
00:24:34,906 --> 00:24:37,534
This money will secure your passage.

378
00:24:37,609 --> 00:24:40,169
I've instructed a man on the west gate
to let you out.

379
00:24:42,647 --> 00:24:43,875
Marian...

380
00:24:48,720 --> 00:24:49,812
Good luck.

381
00:24:51,189 --> 00:24:53,885
Go!

382
00:24:53,959 --> 00:24:55,358
Now!

383
00:24:56,795 --> 00:24:57,762
Excellent.

384
00:25:01,900 --> 00:25:04,960
Taking the lady to see her new lord?

385
00:25:05,670 --> 00:25:07,934
My Lord, I...

386
00:25:08,006 --> 00:25:11,373
As my lieutenant, Gisborne,

387
00:25:11,476 --> 00:25:15,469
you sit at the right hand of the father.

388
00:25:16,581 --> 00:25:21,280
You will share in the fruits of our labor.

389
00:25:21,953 --> 00:25:26,549
You will be a god amongst men,

390
00:25:28,994 --> 00:25:33,363
as long as I can trust you.

391
00:25:38,069 --> 00:25:40,299
Take Lady Marian...

392
00:25:41,306 --> 00:25:43,365
to Winchester.

393
00:25:43,475 --> 00:25:46,035
- Mm.
- Hm?

394
00:25:52,617 --> 00:25:55,814
Er, this? Oh, well, Tunisian, actually.

395
00:25:57,188 --> 00:25:59,884
Yeah, we tour all over the place.

396
00:25:59,958 --> 00:26:02,654
London, Lincoln, Hull.

397
00:26:02,727 --> 00:26:05,855
- Right, come on.
- I'm in the middle of something here.

398
00:26:05,931 --> 00:26:07,865
We have to go and warn Marian.
Now, come on.

399
00:26:07,933 --> 00:26:09,298
Marian?

400
00:26:34,960 --> 00:26:36,689
Guy?

401
00:26:36,761 --> 00:26:37,955
Marian...

402
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:43,024
I'm sorry.

403
00:26:47,172 --> 00:26:49,697
- Sheriff's instructions.
- What?

404
00:26:49,774 --> 00:26:52,265
Get off! Guy!

405
00:26:52,344 --> 00:26:54,539
Get off me, get off me!

406
00:26:54,613 --> 00:26:55,773
Oh! Guy?

407
00:26:59,751 --> 00:27:00,718
Enter.

408
00:27:02,721 --> 00:27:04,518
Ah, the icing on my cake.

409
00:27:04,589 --> 00:27:06,523
Daddy's little girl.

410
00:27:06,591 --> 00:27:08,650
I will not be treated like this.

411
00:27:08,727 --> 00:27:10,217
You're quite right.

412
00:27:11,296 --> 00:27:14,356
These handcuffs and leg irons,
can they be made a little tighter?

413
00:27:14,466 --> 00:27:16,764
- How dare you?
- Oh, gag her, for God's sake.

414
00:27:16,868 --> 00:27:19,462
She's pretty till she talks.
To business. Come along.

415
00:27:27,545 --> 00:27:28,512
Ah!

416
00:27:30,715 --> 00:27:31,682
Marian?

417
00:27:36,955 --> 00:27:38,889
- She's not here.
- What's the problem?

418
00:27:38,957 --> 00:27:40,925
I wanted to talk to her before...

419
00:27:42,127 --> 00:27:43,890
Before what?

420
00:27:44,963 --> 00:27:46,863
What did we have to warn her about?

421
00:27:50,802 --> 00:27:52,429
- Robin...
- Much!

422
00:27:59,511 --> 00:28:00,876
<i>"My dearest Marian,</i>

423
00:28:01,946 --> 00:28:03,538
<i>"I fear we may not meet again</i>

424
00:28:04,983 --> 00:28:06,280
<i>"in this life.</i>

425
00:28:14,192 --> 00:28:16,251
<i>"For the things I did wrong,</i>

426
00:28:18,563 --> 00:28:20,428
<i>"for the things I am about to do,</i>

427
00:28:22,333 --> 00:28:26,292
<i>"but mostly for the life,
for the love we could not have,</i>

428
00:28:29,207 --> 00:28:30,731
<i>"I am truly sorry. "</i>

429
00:28:35,380 --> 00:28:37,143
I want you to give this note to Marian.

430
00:28:37,248 --> 00:28:38,806
What for?

431
00:28:40,852 --> 00:28:44,686
There's been a change of plan.
I want you to wait here for her.

432
00:28:46,458 --> 00:28:49,018
Aren't we supposed to help
you and Winchester escape?

433
00:28:49,094 --> 00:28:51,756
- Yeah, after the show...
- I'll deal with Winchester.

434
00:28:51,863 --> 00:28:54,730
Use the distraction to go down
to the dungeons to release Sir Edward.

435
00:28:54,799 --> 00:28:58,030
Then take him and Marian to the forest.
I'll meet you there.

436
00:28:58,103 --> 00:29:00,435
How are you and Winchester going to escape?

437
00:29:00,505 --> 00:29:02,769
- If the castle guards find you...
- Just do as I say.

438
00:29:05,210 --> 00:29:06,370
Please.

439
00:29:07,879 --> 00:29:09,904
I want you to give me your word.

440
00:29:16,921 --> 00:29:18,616
Good.

441
00:29:27,732 --> 00:29:29,495
And thank you, my friends.

442
00:29:40,612 --> 00:29:42,671
I have a message for you.

443
00:29:42,747 --> 00:29:44,271
From King Richard.

444
00:29:44,349 --> 00:29:45,680
Aah!

445
00:29:51,389 --> 00:29:54,051
I don't like this. I hate it.

446
00:29:54,125 --> 00:29:57,891
It doesn't make sense. If Marian's in
danger, we should be looking for her.

447
00:29:57,962 --> 00:29:59,657
Robin's up to something.

448
00:30:03,301 --> 00:30:04,825
No!

449
00:30:04,903 --> 00:30:07,428
You cannot open people's private letters.

450
00:30:11,109 --> 00:30:12,076
John?

451
00:30:13,778 --> 00:30:14,745
Read it.

452
00:30:27,358 --> 00:30:28,518
Read it for me.

453
00:30:34,332 --> 00:30:36,163
"My dearest Marian,

454
00:30:36,267 --> 00:30:40,260
"I fear we may not meet again in this life. "

455
00:30:41,206 --> 00:30:42,537
What?

456
00:30:42,607 --> 00:30:46,475
"We are both to be betrayed by Winchester. "

457
00:30:46,544 --> 00:30:50,207
<i>"I cannot allow it. All the black knights
will be gathered together -</i>

458
00:30:50,281 --> 00:30:52,010
<i>"Winchester,</i>

459
00:30:52,083 --> 00:30:54,210
<i>"Durham, Rotherham,</i>

460
00:30:54,285 --> 00:30:56,651
<i>"and the rest of the
Sheriff's traitorous gang.</i>

461
00:30:59,123 --> 00:31:01,148
<i>"I may never have the chance again</i>

462
00:31:03,394 --> 00:31:05,760
<i>"and I cannot allow this opportunity to pass.</i>

463
00:31:09,701 --> 00:31:11,066
<i>"I must kill them.</i>

464
00:31:15,473 --> 00:31:19,500
<i>"I only hope you remember me well and forgive
the brutality of what I am going to do.</i>

465
00:31:23,915 --> 00:31:25,906
<i>"If England is to live,</i>

466
00:31:25,984 --> 00:31:27,542
<i>"they must die,</i>

467
00:31:28,386 --> 00:31:29,751
<i>"and so, I fear, must I.</i>

468
00:31:34,158 --> 00:31:36,649
<i>"Go to the woods to fight again.</i>

469
00:31:37,662 --> 00:31:39,721
<i>"Go with my lads.</i>

470
00:31:39,797 --> 00:31:41,458
<i>"I will see you in heaven. "</i>

471
00:31:41,532 --> 00:31:43,557
Let the walls enclose us.

472
00:31:46,604 --> 00:31:47,969
<i>"Goodbye, my love. "</i>

473
00:31:50,708 --> 00:31:54,667
My friends, we are a brotherhood of steel

474
00:31:56,147 --> 00:31:58,115
and our time has come.

475
00:31:59,050 --> 00:32:02,884
As a sign of my unbending fastness
to the cause,

476
00:32:02,954 --> 00:32:05,889
I, Vaizey, Sheriff of this shire,

477
00:32:07,191 --> 00:32:09,455
do add my name

478
00:32:09,527 --> 00:32:11,859
to the great pact of Nottingham.

479
00:32:13,865 --> 00:32:16,299
And I do make my mark.

480
00:32:20,805 --> 00:32:24,070
Next to add his name,

481
00:32:24,142 --> 00:32:26,235
the Lord Winchester.

482
00:32:35,186 --> 00:32:38,246
As a sign of my unbending fastness
to the cause,

483
00:32:38,323 --> 00:32:40,689
I, Harold, Lord of Winchester,

484
00:32:40,758 --> 00:32:43,454
do add my name to this great pact

485
00:32:44,796 --> 00:32:45,820
of Nottingham.

486
00:32:47,999 --> 00:32:51,059
And I do make... my mark.

487
00:32:56,541 --> 00:32:58,532
- Traitors!
- Robin Hood!

488
00:33:05,650 --> 00:33:06,639
Winchester,

489
00:33:06,718 --> 00:33:09,312
the death of every man in this room
is on your head.

490
00:33:11,522 --> 00:33:14,116
Sheriff, Gisborne,

491
00:33:14,192 --> 00:33:15,454
say your prayers.

492
00:33:21,332 --> 00:33:22,526
Hood.

493
00:33:23,901 --> 00:33:25,027
Forgive me.

494
00:33:45,356 --> 00:33:46,880
Guards!

495
00:33:53,731 --> 00:33:56,222
Thank you, my Lord Winchester.

496
00:33:57,735 --> 00:34:00,033
A very good little sweetener indeed.

497
00:34:00,104 --> 00:34:01,332
My pleasure.

498
00:34:01,406 --> 00:34:04,705
Gisborne, don't hang your boy.
I've got a better idea.

499
00:34:05,977 --> 00:34:08,172
Cake on the terrace, gentlemen.

500
00:34:09,147 --> 00:34:11,047
If he dies, I die. If he dies...

501
00:34:11,115 --> 00:34:12,810
Halt. Been looking for you.

502
00:34:14,485 --> 00:34:16,851
What? How come?

503
00:34:16,921 --> 00:34:20,288
The Sheriff wants musicians outside.
They've caught Robin Hood.

504
00:34:47,852 --> 00:34:51,253
Behold the outlaw...

505
00:34:53,558 --> 00:34:55,549
the invincible...

506
00:34:55,660 --> 00:34:58,060
and legendary Robin Hood,

507
00:34:58,129 --> 00:35:01,155
and his friend Allan A Dale.

508
00:35:02,700 --> 00:35:05,897
How fitting, then, that these two renegades,

509
00:35:05,970 --> 00:35:07,835
these enemies of the law,

510
00:35:07,905 --> 00:35:11,966
which make them enemies
of good King Richard himself,

511
00:35:12,076 --> 00:35:16,035
should provide us with entertainment
on this, the day of the King's birthday.

512
00:35:16,114 --> 00:35:17,206
Huh?

513
00:35:17,281 --> 00:35:20,341
Thank you, legendary Robin Hood.

514
00:35:22,987 --> 00:35:26,650
Now the game is very simple. Fight or fry.

515
00:35:26,724 --> 00:35:29,887
Hm? Ha-ha!
And of course the winner gets his freedom.

516
00:35:29,961 --> 00:35:31,758
Cake!

517
00:35:34,565 --> 00:35:36,430
Enjoy! Ha-ha!

518
00:35:38,369 --> 00:35:39,529
Mm.

519
00:35:39,604 --> 00:35:41,367
Poke him, poke him!

520
00:35:47,178 --> 00:35:49,373
You don't have to do this, Allan.

521
00:35:49,480 --> 00:35:51,539
Don't give them the satisfaction.

522
00:35:51,649 --> 00:35:53,549
Even if you do kill me,
they won't let you go.

523
00:35:53,651 --> 00:35:54,948
Come on, poke him.

524
00:35:55,052 --> 00:35:57,213
If you had listened,
you might have understood.

525
00:35:58,923 --> 00:36:00,686
You should have given me a second chance.

526
00:36:13,905 --> 00:36:16,703
- How did you get to be so low?
- That was always your problem.

527
00:36:16,774 --> 00:36:18,537
So high and mighty, eh?

528
00:36:18,609 --> 00:36:21,271
- So much better than everyone else.
- No.

529
00:36:21,345 --> 00:36:22,642
Just better than you.

530
00:36:35,493 --> 00:36:36,687
Careful!

531
00:37:01,485 --> 00:37:02,509
Ah.

532
00:37:02,587 --> 00:37:07,251
Well, it looks like our little Robin Redbreast
is just about to become fried chicken!

533
00:37:10,328 --> 00:37:12,262
Ooh, I like this. Yes, very good.

534
00:37:16,133 --> 00:37:18,328
- Music!
- I'll give him music!

535
00:37:19,070 --> 00:37:20,037
Go!

536
00:37:23,708 --> 00:37:24,766
Get them!

537
00:37:25,910 --> 00:37:27,571
Charge!

538
00:37:31,749 --> 00:37:34,217
- Robin!
- Stop them!

539
00:37:42,493 --> 00:37:44,017
John. Friends.

540
00:37:45,696 --> 00:37:47,027
Traitor!

541
00:37:48,099 --> 00:37:49,862
I let you in but I'm not letting you out.

542
00:37:55,673 --> 00:37:57,334
Told you I was good with wood.

543
00:37:59,510 --> 00:38:00,670
Time to disappear.

544
00:38:04,081 --> 00:38:05,275
What's he doing now?

545
00:38:11,355 --> 00:38:12,549
Oh, no!

546
00:38:18,896 --> 00:38:20,056
This way!

547
00:38:26,003 --> 00:38:27,834
Stop!

548
00:38:31,208 --> 00:38:32,470
Let's go, let's go!

549
00:38:37,882 --> 00:38:39,110
Guards!

550
00:38:45,189 --> 00:38:48,352
Well, you said it'd be entertaining,

551
00:38:48,459 --> 00:38:50,359
but that was really something.

552
00:38:50,461 --> 00:38:52,122
And once again, gentlemen,

553
00:38:52,196 --> 00:38:54,130
it's a pleasure doing business with you.

554
00:38:54,198 --> 00:38:55,631
Bring the girl.

555
00:38:55,700 --> 00:38:56,689
Marian.

556
00:38:58,536 --> 00:38:59,969
Marian!

557
00:39:02,573 --> 00:39:04,666
I'm surprised you gave into his demands.

558
00:39:04,742 --> 00:39:06,573
I had to get his signature.

559
00:39:09,146 --> 00:39:10,238
But now...

560
00:39:11,315 --> 00:39:13,613
I have his signature.

561
00:39:16,087 --> 00:39:17,486
I'll send a squad of men.

562
00:39:17,555 --> 00:39:18,954
No.

563
00:39:19,056 --> 00:39:22,048
No, we do this one quietly.

564
00:39:22,126 --> 00:39:24,060
Bring your boy.

565
00:39:44,482 --> 00:39:46,245
Home.

566
00:40:00,931 --> 00:40:02,296
Here they come.

567
00:40:04,101 --> 00:40:06,968
Get your hands off me.

568
00:40:07,071 --> 00:40:08,936
Spirit!

569
00:40:09,006 --> 00:40:10,837
Just like your mother.

570
00:40:10,908 --> 00:40:13,035
Will, you take out the two outriders.

571
00:40:13,110 --> 00:40:14,304
Much, John, Djaq,

572
00:40:14,378 --> 00:40:16,346
you cover me while I rescue Marian.

573
00:40:17,148 --> 00:40:18,672
What are they doing?

574
00:40:18,749 --> 00:40:20,148
They're stopping.

575
00:40:24,955 --> 00:40:26,320
Why have we stopped?

576
00:40:30,661 --> 00:40:33,653
- It's you!
- Yes, me.

577
00:40:33,731 --> 00:40:36,063
Did you really think

578
00:40:36,133 --> 00:40:38,567
that I would just smile
and let you have Sussex?

579
00:40:38,669 --> 00:40:40,660
A clue.

580
00:40:41,338 --> 00:40:42,771
No.

581
00:40:43,808 --> 00:40:45,139
Hm?

582
00:40:49,513 --> 00:40:50,445
Marian!

583
00:40:59,957 --> 00:41:02,755
A little sweetener for you,

584
00:41:02,860 --> 00:41:04,691
a little bonus.

585
00:41:10,968 --> 00:41:12,458
- You're safe now.
- Thank you.

586
00:41:19,977 --> 00:41:22,172
Sweet, very sweet.

587
00:41:41,565 --> 00:41:42,532
What?

588
00:41:43,300 --> 00:41:45,564
I'm trying to think of the good bit.

589
00:41:45,669 --> 00:41:48,229
Even on a bad day
there's always something good.

590
00:41:49,406 --> 00:41:50,771
It's what my mother used to say.

591
00:41:52,009 --> 00:41:54,910
But today, Winchester's betrayed us,

592
00:41:54,979 --> 00:41:57,948
the pact's been signed,
Allan is Gisborne's man,

593
00:41:58,048 --> 00:42:00,243
Marian's galloped off...

594
00:42:04,588 --> 00:42:07,056
- I mean, help me out here cos I'm struggling.
- Much...

595
00:42:07,124 --> 00:42:08,853
Shut up.

596
00:42:15,566 --> 00:42:17,124
Robin's alive.

597
00:42:17,201 --> 00:42:18,862
That's a good thing.

598
00:42:18,936 --> 00:42:21,666
That's a very good thing,
cos for a minute that was looking...

599
00:42:21,739 --> 00:42:23,468
Shut up, Much!

600
00:42:27,912 --> 00:42:29,880
- And if I may say so...
- Much, shut up!

601
00:42:35,319 --> 00:42:37,787
- We can't just eat in silence.
- Shut up, Much!

